WEBVTT

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.410
F-Faria?

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.280
What are you...

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.340
U-Um...

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.340
I-I'm sorry for startling you.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.950
Oh, no, that was on me...

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.850
You were trying to wipe my brow.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.050
You were in bed a whole day.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.860
You used up too much magic.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.360
I guess that makes sense.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.330
I won't give up!

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.240
But... how's Gildan?

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.220
He's fine.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.800
He actually woke up before you did.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.010
That's great.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.130
I'm so glad he's safe.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.990
Is that all?

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:25.680
You almost died, you know?

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.690
It wouldn't hurt to be a little more 
concerned about yourself.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.860
R-Right...

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.140
I've been thinking this for a while...

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.480
You push yourself too hard.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.040
Do I?

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.840
Yes, you do.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.430
You did it with Jou, and with Gildan.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.360
I'll acknowledge that your 
actions did save them both,

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.680
but in the future, that won't necessarily—

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.070
Excuse me. What are you doing?

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.560
Huh? What am I doing?

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.410
Now that I'm awake, 
I can't just stay in bed all day...

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:09.290
You can and you <i>should</i>!

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.980
Ellen said you need more rest.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.490
Um...

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:22.240
I've made up my mind!

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.430
Until you've completely recovered,

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.750
I shall remain right here
 and take care of you!

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.750
Huh?

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:08.410
<b>Friendship\h\h\h-Connection-</b>

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.830
Not that I mind...

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:09.220
But its a little stuffy 
in here with just us guys.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.980
I'm glad you're feeling 
well enough for snark.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:19.280
Oh? Dissatisfied with our 
courteous care, Your Highness?

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.650
Yeah, yeah. I want for nothing.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.990
I'm jealous of Nemo, getting the 
president looking after him...

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.000
Anyway, is it true you don't recall
what transpired before your possession?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.680
Y-Yeah...

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.630
The next thing I knew, 
I was locked in that state.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.390
I see...

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.900
Somethin' on your mind?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.040
Possession itself is a 
frequent enough occurrence.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:00.970
But the onset seemed awfully 
sudden for a man of your caliber.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.360
You think something's weird about it?

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:09.020
Unless it was caused by some outside influence.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.740
Hang on a minute. Are you sayin'...

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:15.450
Somebody was there to trigger it?

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:16.510
Physis?!

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.250
I-Inside the academy?

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.730
It's only a theory.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.490
But thinking back on it,

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.480
it's curious that dragon you brought in

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.810
came back to life so quickly as well.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.760
All of this is happening on school grounds.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.460
Which means...

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.890
Hoo boy, not again.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:43.200
The president really is hopeless.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.300
Maybe I'm not so jealous anymore.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.970
The pot! The pot of porridge...

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:54.140
What do I do? What do I do? What do I do?

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.240
Um, Faria, you can just reduce the heat—

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.040
That's right!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.080
Hey! Back to bed with you!

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.270
R-Right.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.610
I'm sorry.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.620
I ended up making croquettes.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:15.310
It's just the only thing I'm any good at...

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.570
No, these are just fine.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:26.470
I really like your croquettes.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.320
Th-Thank you.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.060
A cat?

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:49.880
It has a collar.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.420
Is it someone's pet?

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.920
Wait a minute...

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.610
Um, you see...

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:07.480
She's usually in my room, 
but I guess she came looking for me.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.080
Hey, now!

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:14.870
There, there.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:18.330
<i>I've never seen her like this.</i>

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:22.400
Oh, would you like to pet her, Nemo?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.210
May I?

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.840
That's odd.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.060
I've never seen her so worked up...

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.980
I guess she's afraid of me.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:03.270
Forgive me. I need a break.

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:07.040
No, that's okay...

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.850
President?

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.330
You really need to get back to work.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.010
You're right.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:27.190
Not everything is up to my discretion.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.990
I prefer to go with the flow, after all.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:37.200
And we need your findings on the 
hourglasses for the chairman's debriefing.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.700
I need to tend to things. Do you mind?

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:44.050
Just make sure you stay right there, okay?

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:52.670
I wonder who's really looking after whom.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.430
Sorry. I just slipped a bit.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.330
You clearly haven't been sleeping well.

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:01.880
If your duties are getting too taxing,

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:04.730
you should delegate! 
To someone who isn't me!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.940
You know I can't do that.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.540
I'm a hands-on kind of person.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.130
I do worry about her.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.310
If she has it that hard, 
why does she bother with me?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.950
It's just in her nature.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.410
Have some.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:32.970
Th-Thanks.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:39.790
That's great.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.120
Glad to hear it.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:46.150
Have you known Faria a long time, Ellen?

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.980
Well, long enough.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:56.490
The legendary knight Eunomia 
was an ancestor of hers,

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:01.990
so she's been trained as a Seven Knights
 successor since childhood.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:12.970
She wants to protect everything
with her hero's power.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.530
That is amazing.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:20.340
But then she surely doesn't need
 to focus so much on me.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.140
Oh, but she does.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:28.480
You're of special importance to her.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:36.230
Because you were the only 
survivor of that village.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.860
She's regretted it all this time...

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.820
Not being able to save your hometown.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.420
You shall not lay a hand on him!

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.520
You okay?

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:13.790
I'm so glad... I could save at least you.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.790
I think she feels a strong sense 
of responsibility for you,

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.380
the lone survivor.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:28.500
She really doesn't have to, though...

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:35.340
Am I really just a burden on her?

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:50.980
Nemo?

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:52.520
Come in.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.430
Hey, Nemo! Got some time to kill?

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:00.310
We came to check on you.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:00.990
Hey!

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.530
Guys! And Gildan, too!

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.990
Are you feeling better?

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:06.410
Just fine.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.990
Jive and I are getting along 
better than ever, too.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.250
I guess I owe you one.

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:15.660
You're totally like the
 president's pet now, Nemo.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.960
Oh, I'm not Faria's pet. That's—

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.260
N-Nemo!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.440
C'mon.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.200
Actin' like a chick right outta the egg...

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.810
To see the man I trust 
my life with reduced to this...

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:30.020
My, I see we have quite a crowd.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.560
M-M-M-M-Miss Sophitia?!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.600
Such a pleasure to see you this day!

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.520
Who's reduced to what now?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.210
So, what's that?

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:44.450
A secret elven decoction.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.820
It's been used to speed 
recoveries since ancient times.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.040
Th-Thanks...

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.240
We're all counting on you.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.990
Return to the Seven Knights' 
battlefield as soon as possible.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.420
You're pretty good at this nursing thing.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.480
Indeed.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:00.510
Yes! And our bud—

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:03.070
I mean, our friend Nemo is a pretty cool—

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:04.820
I mean, a very reliable comrade, too!

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.150
My, my. Is he now?

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:11.990
Well, if you ever need anything, 
do stop by the library.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.140
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.570
Is it this one? Or is it this one?

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.000
Oh, not that one.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.080
Thanks for telling me...

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.090
As if I'd fall for that!

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:43.710
You gotta be kidding me!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.400
I lost!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.270
The prince loses three in a row.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.850
A spectacular bluff.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.810
That was impressive, Nemo.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.350
Well, I told you so...

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:54.890
Ah, jeez...

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:58.100
Maybe I'll ask Jive for advice in the future.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.860
Consulting your hero
 over something so trivial?

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.810
Good idea! I like it!

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:06.750
But me and Spike will be the 
ultimate team in any game you name!

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.610
Not you too, Jou!

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.130
That's right...
 You can all talk to your heroes.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.940
You still can't speak with your hero?

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.630
No. I only hear him talk to me.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:24.220
But you get such power from him...

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.880
We all assumed you could 
communicate with your hero.

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:30.860
Speaking of, you said 
you don't even know his name?

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.640
There might be an abnormality.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:35.710
Gareth!

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.170
No, it's okay.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:39.390
He could be right.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:42.140
Ever consider askin' Miss Sophitia?

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:45.900
She's a librarian, so she knows lots
 about the heroes' roots.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.410
I'll think about it.

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:59.160
You're all disturbing the peace.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:05.500
To think the Seven Knights would be goofing 
off past bedtime at such a busy time...

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.800
The disciplinary board has arrived.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.090
I'm sorry.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:11.680
It was my idea. 
I thought it might lift Nemo's spirits.

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:18.810
I understand. I also know you, President.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.560
You're already busy enough.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.680
You don't need to be taking 
on additional burdens.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.180
I know, but—

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:31.100
You must conserve your energy.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.400
Remember the grave situation we're in.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.570
I think she's mad.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.960
Maybe keep it down 
 to a dull roar in the future, man.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.460
The grave situation we're in, she says?

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.260
Perhaps she's right.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.710
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.030
I'll tidy up.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:55.740
Nemo...

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.890
There really is something strange about him.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:01.920
You still can't speak with your hero?

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.490
The fact that he can't communicate 
with his hero bothers me.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:06.680
But...

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.570
I suppose I'm hiding a few things myself.

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:19.080
I expected you'd drop by sooner or later.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.890
I'm glad to see you feeling better.

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:30.660
Yeah.

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.220
Is something the matter, Nemo?

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.930
Say, Faria, am I—

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.030
You! What are you doing here?

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.140
Wh-What'll I do?

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:44.910
What's wrong?

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.500
We're not actually allowed 
to have pets in the dorm.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:47.900
What?

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.850
If Shirley and the others find out...

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.660
W-We'd better catch her.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:07.860
Oh! Oh no!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:15.010
How shall we handle the budget report
 for the school festival?

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.040
I'll let you take point.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:20.230
What are you two doing?

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.680
Oh, you know...

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.920
Just some... rehab stretches?

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.650
What is it?

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.540
Let's hurry, Faria.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.610
Y-Yes.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.740
Wait!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:46.300
Say, you think they're hooking up?

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:47.910
Don't be rude, Mina.

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:51.540
<i>They're definitely hiding something.</i>

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.170
Now's our chance.

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:22.830
Okay, but...

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.330
She's still scared of me.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.050
Oh, no!

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.430
We have to help her!

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:54.650
Nemo!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.090
You're pushing yourself again.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:14.710
You're going to fall, too!

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.130
Let me go!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:18.880
No! I'll never let go!

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.020
Why are you so desperate to save me?

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.640
I don't want to be a burden on you.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.890
I'm just not someone who can let go.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.390
And you certainly aren't a burden.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:33.400
I'm doing this because I want to...

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:38.810
Because I want to be your friend!

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:42.660
I...

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.080
I still can't talk freely with him...

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.330
But I think he told me to do what I wanted.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:42.790
Little bugs who have never seen the sky...

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:49.900
Rush across the land on a journey...

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:57.520
Down an endless road...

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:04.270
That you found in a dream...

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:11.120
Little birds who have never seen the sea...

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.170
<i>I understand your doubts, Faria.</i>

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:18.030
Take flight and ride the wind...

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.290
Lady Eunomia?

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:17.420
<i>A storm is coming.</i>

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.040
<i>A great tempest.</i>

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:25.320
Embrace a love that echoes...

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:24.180
<i>It is not the heroes of old who can 
protect the world from this storm.</i>

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.320
<i>It is you, the living.</i>

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:32.310
Deep inside your heart...

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:50.610
I want to know...

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:53.370
about my hero.

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:27.550
Shirley's stone cold.

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:28.930
That's just a front I put up.

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:30.980
We're counting on you as head 
of the disciplinary committee.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:33.290
I'm nothing if not reliable.

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:34.910
Oh my goodness!

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:36.890
Next time: "Physis."

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Rampancy -Physis-</b>

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:39.320
But you're still Shirley, aren't you?
